Subject: [DEBUG, test builds only] PCI: qcom: run-time switch to let the root ports go to D3hot in system suspend

Not for release builds.  scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh applies this only
with both APPLY_DEEP_SLEEP_DEBUG_SWITCHES=1 and
APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_GUARD=1, on top of
pcie-qcom-keep-power-domain-while-link-kept.patch, and refuses any other
build in a source tree that carries it.  No board check.

One switch, which root writes at run time and nothing else changes:

  /sys/module/pcie_qcom/parameters/debug_root_port_d3   N at every boot

Y gives each root port of a qcom PCIe host bridge_d3, the PCI core's
permission for a bridge to go to D3hot, where the PCI core gave it none;
N takes it away again.  From the next system suspend such a root port goes
to D3hot once the functions below it are (pci_pm_suspend_noirq(): a bridge
is put in a low-power state only with bridge_d3, pci_power_manageable()),
the host then finds every function in D3hot, sends PME_Turn_Off and powers
itself down (dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(), pci_host_common_d3cold_possible()),
and with the guard genpd collapses pcie_0_gdsc; the resume sets the host up
again, trains the link, and the PCI core restores the root port's and the
functions' configuration (pci_pm_resume_noirq()); ath11k powers its chip
down and up at every suspend anyway (its default PM policy).  It is what a
sleep with the PCIe root port removed (sleep-test.sh pci=remove) does with
the Wi-Fi kept: tools/inplace/typec-roles/sleep-test.sh root-port-d3 sets it
for a pci=keep run.

Why the PCI core gives none: the SM8550's root ports are hot-plug capable
(33a76fc3c3e6, v7.1), and pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 to a
hot-plug port that pciehp does not handle natively before it looks at
pcie_port_pm=force (drivers/pci/pci.c); this kernel has CONFIG_ACPI=y and
no CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE, so pciehp_is_native() is false.  d4c79b63d82
(v7.3) lifts the check after that one, for non-x86, and does not help
without pciehp.  The community SM8550 kernels build pciehp in and boot with
pcie_port_pm=force (ROCKNIX); a kernel configuration change is what this
switch avoids, and it can be tried inside the sleep test's protection
first.

Refused before SYSTEM_RUNNING (-EPERM), so the kernel command line cannot
set it: the boot's pm_test=platform panel cycle keeps the link.  A Y that
finds no such root port (sleep-test.sh pci=remove took it away) gets
-ENODEV.  A root port whose D3 the PCI core allows itself is left alone.
bridge_d3 is recomputed only for a port the PCI core can put in D3 itself
(pci_bridge_d3_update()), so nothing but an N changes it back before the
restart.  It is a bit-field next to others the PCI core writes in a suspend
or from sysfs (skip_bus_pm, d3cold_allowed); the write is made with the
system running and before a run, under pci_lock_rescan_remove(), which
guards against a removal and not against those, none of which runs then.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2422,3 +2422,85 @@
 	},
 };
 builtin_platform_driver(qcom_pcie_driver);
+
+/*
+ * PCIe root port to D3 for a sleep test, not for release builds:
+ * pcie_qcom.debug_root_port_d3, which scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh adds
+ * only with APPLY_DEEP_SLEEP_DEBUG_SWITCHES=1 and
+ * APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_GUARD=1 (pcie-qcom-debug-root-port-d3.patch).
+ *
+ * A host powers itself down in a system suspend only when every function
+ * on its bus is in D3hot, its root port included
+ * (pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(), from dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()).  The
+ * root port goes to D3hot only when the PCI core gave it bridge_d3
+ * (pci_power_manageable(), from pci_pm_suspend_noirq()), which it gives a
+ * root port that is hot-plug capable, as the SM8550's are (33a76fc3c3e6),
+ * only when pciehp handles it: CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE, which this kernel
+ * leaves out, and pcie_port_pm=force or d4c79b63d82 (pci_bridge_d3_possible(),
+ * drivers/pci/pci.c).  So with the Wi-Fi bound the host keeps its link in
+ * every suspend.  Y gives each root port of a qcom PCIe host that the PCI
+ * core keeps in D0 bridge_d3 until the restart or an N: from the next
+ * suspend it goes to D3hot after its functions, the host sends PME_Turn_Off
+ * and powers down, and its resume sets the host up again, trains the link
+ * and restores the functions' configuration (pci_pm_resume_noirq()).  It is
+ * that switch alone: whether the Wi-Fi comes back from it is what a run with
+ * it is for (tools/inplace/typec-roles/sleep-test.sh root-port-d3).  Root
+ * writes it at run time; the kernel command line cannot (-EPERM before
+ * SYSTEM_RUNNING): the boot's pm_test=platform panel cycle keeps the link.
+ * A Y finds no such port (pci=remove took it away): -ENODEV.  The PCI core
+ * recomputes bridge_d3 only for a port it can put in D3 itself
+ * (pci_bridge_d3_update()), so nothing changes it back but N; it is a
+ * bit-field next to others that the PCI core writes in a suspend or from
+ * sysfs, which this write, made before a run, does not meet.
+ */
+static bool qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3;
+
+static int qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	struct pci_dev *pdev = NULL;
+	bool on;
+	int ret, n = 0;
+
+	/* Run time only: see above. */
+	if (system_state != SYSTEM_RUNNING)
+		return -EPERM;
+
+	ret = kstrtobool(val, &on);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	pci_lock_rescan_remove();
+	for_each_pci_dev(pdev) {
+		struct pci_host_bridge *bridge;
+
+		if (!pci_is_pcie(pdev) || pci_pcie_type(pdev) != PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+			continue;
+		bridge = pci_find_host_bridge(pdev->bus);
+		if (!bridge || !bridge->dev.parent ||
+		    bridge->dev.parent->driver != &qcom_pcie_driver.driver)
+			continue;
+		/* A port the PCI core can put in D3 itself is left to it. */
+		if (pci_bridge_d3_possible(pdev))
+			continue;
+		pdev->bridge_d3 = on;
+		pci_info(pdev, "debug: %s in system suspend (pcie_qcom.debug_root_port_d3 %c)\n",
+			 on ? "goes to D3hot" : "stays in D0", on ? 'Y' : 'N');
+		n++;
+	}
+	pci_unlock_rescan_remove();
+
+	if (on && !n)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	*(bool *)kp->arg = on;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3_ops = {
+	.set = qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3_set,
+	.get = param_get_bool,
+};
+
+module_param_cb(debug_root_port_d3, &qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3_ops, &qcom_pcie_debug_rp_d3, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug_root_port_d3,
+		 "debug: Y: the root ports of qcom PCIe hosts go to D3hot in system suspend (run time only)");
